      "content": "I'd recommend offering a partial credit or a significant discount on a future purchase instead of a full refund. You can frame this as an exception to policy, acknowledging the damage while subtly shifting the focus to customer retention. This demonstrates good faith without absorbing the full cost of the breakage, which is a common carrier issue. This approach keeps the customer feeling valued while protecting your bottom line.",
